# Pin: tools/deslop_kz.py --host over koru_std at --min-tokens=48,
# measured 2026-10-14. The OTHER census: the .kz layer is Zig host text —
# canon's host_line/proc-body strings are opaque to the decl census, so
# this mode reassembles each file's Zig as a synthetic .zig and runs the
# SAME token-normalized fingerprint (tools/deslop.zig) over it. First
# measured baseline: the layer holds ~15x the clone mass the decl census
# ever saw (1061 clusters vs 70). Keys are ceilings; see the sibling
# baselines. Six files' host text does not parse standalone
# (eval/table/types/control/declarations/io — dormant proc bodies carry
# Zig that never reached a compiler, e.g. `.{ .error = ... }`); they are
# named on stderr and escape the count until they parse.
# Tightened 2026-10-14 same-day: the refusal-envelope fold (122 sites,
# `.replacement = ast.refusal(...)` longhand -> ast.refuse) collapsed the
# board's largest cross-file idiom. Net -19 clusters/-43 members vs the
# first pin; the +2/+2 over the fold's own measurement is concurrent
# pump/channel churn in the working tree, not the fold.
# 1045/889: +3 clusters over 1042 is a concurrent session's uncommitted
# interpreter/bridge/runtime edits in the shared checkout — clean HEAD
# measures exactly 1042. Re-pinned to measured per the uncommitted-work
# clause; re-settles when that work commits.
clusters=1027
members=891
# 1027/891: module-home dedupe deleted five private copies of the
# moduleHome/containingFlow walks (-18 clusters, the copies WERE clones);
# +2 members are the new home parts' fns twinning existing shells.
